(b) IDs right-aligned to a fixed width so the titles line up in a column.
(c) Due dates shown in their own aligned column, or as "(due YYYY-MM-DD)" after the title.
(d) Done todos shown differently (dimmed, struck through, or listed separately).
(e) A header line or a summary, like "3 todos, 1 done".
(f) A friendly message such as "No todos." when the list is empty.
(g) ANSI colours. Should these turn off when the output isn't a terminal?
If you can, write an example of what the output should look like for a few todos (one done, one with a due date).

